1
00:04:50,526 --> 00:04:56,526
Guess who just made number two?

2
00:09:41,052 --> 00:09:47,052
Jackass Number Two is a action, comedy,
documentary film directed by Jeff Tremaine.

3
00:14:31,578 --> 00:14:37,578
Jackass Number Two is a compilation of various stunts,
pranks and skits, and essentially has no plot.

4
00:19:22,105 --> 00:19:28,105
Chris Pontius, Johnny Knoxville, Steve-O, Bam Margera, and the whole crew
return to the screen to raise the stakes higher than ever before.

5
00:24:12,631 --> 00:24:18,631
Self, played by Johnny Knoxville.

6
00:29:03,157 --> 00:29:09,157
Self, played by Bam Margera.

7
00:33:53,684 --> 00:33:59,684
Self, played by Steve-O.

8
00:38:44,210 --> 00:38:50,210
Self, played by Chris Pontius.

9
00:43:34,736 --> 00:43:40,736
Self, played by Ryan Dunn.

10
00:48:25,263 --> 00:48:31,263
Self, played by Jason 'Wee Man' Acuña.

11
00:53:15,789 --> 00:53:21,789
Jackass Number Two is a 2006 American reality slapstick comedy film directed by Jeff
Tremaine, and produced by Tremaine, Spike Jonze, and Johnny Knoxville.

12
00:58:06,315 --> 00:58:12,315
It is the sequel to Jackass: The Movie (2002), both
based upon the MTV series Jackass.

13
01:02:56,842 --> 01:03:02,842
Like its predecessor and the original television show, the film is a compilation of stunts, pranks and skits, starring the regular Jackass cast
of Johnny Knoxville, Bam Margera, Dave England, Ryan Dunn, Chris Pontius, Wee Man, Steve-O, Preston Lacy, and Ehren McGhehey.

14
01:07:47,368 --> 01:07:53,368
Produced by MTV Films, Dickhouse Productions and Lynch Siderow Productions, and distributed by Paramount Pictures, the film premiered in theaters on September
22, 2006, received generally positive reviews from critics and grossed $84.6 million worldwide against a production budget of $11.5 million.

15
01:12:37,894 --> 01:12:43,894
Unused material of the film was released as a separate movie titled Jackass 2.5
online on December 19, 2007, and on DVD on December 26, 2007.

16
01:17:28,421 --> 01:17:34,421
It was followed by another sequel, Jackass 3D (2010).

17
01:22:18,947 --> 01:22:24,947
The film explores themes of pain, wound, disgust, stunt, stuntman.

18
01:27:09,473 --> 01:27:15,473
The tone is lighthearted.
